<h1>The Big One — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 27, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>The Big One (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.thebigone</code>) is the daily publication of Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley), Abbeville, Louisiana. Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>The Big One collects <strong>no data</strong>. No accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no advertising SDK, no tracking — we never see what you read. The edition is bundled inside the app and reads fully offline. The app's only permission is internet access, used for exactly one thing, described below.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Reading is offline.</strong> Each edition — its seven departments, its puzzle, its pictures — is stored inside the app itself. Your reading progress and puzzle state are remembered in the app on your own device only, so a finished edition stays finished. That information never leaves your phone.</li>
  <li><strong>The weather now-line refreshes live.</strong> When your phone is online, the app asks the public weather service Open-Meteo for the current conditions in <strong>Abbeville, Louisiana — our hometown, printed on the masthead</strong>. That request is for one fixed place, the same for every reader. The app holds no location permission, never asks where you are, and sends nothing about you: no name, no identifier, nothing you typed (the app has no fields to type into). Offline, the figures printed in the edition simply stand.</li>
  <li><strong>The Root Checker line.</strong> Like every app in our house, The Big One carries a built-in Root Checker. It looks at your device, on your device, and prints what it finds on the edition's colophon line for you to see — for example whether root was detected and how many game controllers are connected. That report is shown to you and <strong>never sent anywhere</strong>; the checker has no network path. Root and controllers are welcome in our house; the checker watches, it never blocks.</li>
  <li><strong>Doors out open in your browser.</strong> The app includes links: the Documentary shelf at the Internet Archive, our subscription register and sister apps on our own website, and a PayPal tip jar. Those links open in your <strong>system browser</strong>, outside the app. If you follow one, whatever you do on that site is under that site's own privacy policy; the app itself sends nothing anywhere.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Only your reading progress and puzzle state, on your device, as described above. We receive nothing and keep nothing. Uninstalling the app erases them.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet</strong> — for the single weather refresh described above, and for nothing else. No other permission is requested. In particular, the app has <strong>no location permission</strong> and cannot know where you are.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>This app contains <strong>no advertising SDK, no ad network, and no advertising ID</strong>, and collects nothing for advertising. Each edition carries a clearly labeled <strong>House Promo</strong> card that rotates notes about our own other publications and apps, and a labeled Sponsor chair; both are printed as part of the edition itself, load nothing from any network, and track nothing. If a real third-party ad build ever ships, this policy and the app's Google Play declarations will be updated first.</p>

<h2>Subscriptions and payments</h2>
<p>The Big One sells nothing inside the app and takes no payment information. Subscriptions are kept at the register on our website; the app only carries the door (a browser link). We never see or store your card details.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The Big One is a publication for adults — its target audience is readers 18 and over — and it is not directed at children. It collects no data from anyone, of any age. Our child-directed apps (the Kids' Corner line) are separate products with their own policies.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

